&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is a 12-week internship during summer 2027.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join the Crypto Inventory Operations team within Finance, which is responsible for monitoring Coinbase&#39;s operational crypto balances, supporting inventory operations processes, and improving controls and workflows across the business. As a Crypto Inventory Operations Intern, you&#39;ll gain exposure to how a leading crypto company manages crypto assets at scale. You&#39;ll work alongside experienced treasury professionals and partner with Product, Engineering, Accounting, Compliance, and Operations teams to help reduce operational risk, improve controls, and keep financial workflows running smoothly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support daily crypto inventory operations by monitoring balances across Coinbase entities, assisting with data gathering for inventory activities, and escalating items that require follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with the stablecoin process by monitoring balances and thresholds, reviewing alerts, and coordinating follow-up actions with Engineering partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Unclaimed Property operations by updating and maintaining tracking spreadsheets, organizing/saving supporting documents, and assisting with due diligence activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and improve dashboards, trackers, and reporting tools that increase visibility into crypto inventory, P&amp;amp;L exposure, and workflow status&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute research and process-improvement projects focused on reducing idle balances, improving automation, and documenting operational procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to enhance operational workflows using automation and AI tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently pursuing a Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics, Business Administration, or a related discipline with an expected graduation between December 2027 and June 2028&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated interest in crypto assets, digital asset operations, corporate treasury, accounting, or fintech through coursework, prior internships, or personal projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Microsoft Excel or Google Sheets with the ability to build and maintain operational models and trackers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills with the ability to document procedures, investigate issues, and present findings to cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, control quality, and documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Position ID: P78090&lt;/p&gt;
