&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a CX Trading Program Manager on the CX Programs team within Customer Experience, you&#39;ll own the end-to-end support experience across Coinbase&#39;s trading products, including the differentiated service model for our highest-value trading customers. You&#39;ll bridge Trading product teams and CX operations to reduce customer friction, ensure smooth product launches, and drive retention for the customers who matter most to our trading business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a portfolio of trading product domains, including support contact rate reduction targets, launch readiness, and performance scorecards across approximately half of the global trading CX scope&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the high net worth CX program end-to-end, defining segment strategy, retention priorities, the service model, and the cross-functional operating model spanning Sales, Concierge, Compliance/Risk, and Trading product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set program strategy and prioritization frameworks for ambiguous, high-stakes problems, influencing Director+ stakeholders to align on tradeoffs, resources, and sequencing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute a multi-quarter improvement roadmap that combines in-product fixes with CX-owned improvements through automation, help center content, and proactive support to reduce top contact drivers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute CX readiness for Tier 1 trading launches, coordinating across Product, WFM, L&amp;amp;D, and Tooling, then measuring post-launch impact on CSAT, contact volume, and adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Trading product teams through regular operational reviews that surface voice-of-customer themes, quantify business impact, and close performance gaps with executive-ready reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in program management, CX, or product operations, with 5+ years in a trading, brokerage, or financial services environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record owning a high-value customer segment or business-critical program where retention, revenue, or market share were explicit success metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to define strategy and lead complex cross-functional programs spanning 5+ teams (including Sales, Compliance, and BPO partners) with measurable business outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience influencing Director+ stakeholders, negotiating priorities across competing initiatives, and driving alignment without direct authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency defining KPI frameworks, OKR glidepaths, and executive reporting that connects CX performance metrics to revenue and retention impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active FINRA Series 7 and Series 63 licenses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
