&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is a 12-week internship during summer 2027.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a Product Manager Intern to join the HR Technology team within People Success and help drive key initiatives across our HR Technology ecosystem, from evaluating AI-powered tools to automating core processes and strengthening our security foundation. You&#39;ll ship real products, partnering with HR, IT, and Security stakeholders to design and deliver tools that transform how our employees work. You&#39;ll own projects end-to-end and gain hands-on experience on a team building an AI-native HR organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a product initiative from discovery to launch, including build vs. buy analysis, workflow redesign, or feature adoption for a new HR Technology tool&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with HR, IT, Security, and vendor teams to define requirements, gather user feedback, and align stakeholders on product priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the evaluation and piloting of generative AI agents for HR teams, defining success metrics and tracking ROI for AI-powered tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Map existing workflows, identify bottlenecks, and implement automated solutions using our HRIS, applicant tracking system, and enterprise collaboration platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze product metrics and user data to measure impact, inform decisions, and communicate results to leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently pursuing a degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Management Information Systems, Business, Human-Computer Interaction, or a related field, or have equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated analytical and problem-solving ability, such as structuring ambiguous problems into clear action plans in academic projects, case competitions, or prior internships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with AI tools, prompt engineering, or low-code/no-code platforms (e.g., building automated workflows, prototyping with LLM-based applications, or working with APIs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage a project from start to finish, including defining scope, tracking milestones, and delivering outcomes on deadline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;History of proactively identifying problems and proposing solutions, such as surfacing process gaps, pitching improvements, or initiating projects without being asked, in academic, extracurricular, or professional settings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
