&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a Product Manager II within Coinbase’s Identity organization and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers/product-groups&quot;&gt;Platform&lt;/a&gt; group, you&#39;ll own the strategy and execution for enterprise identity and multi-user experiences across Coinbase&#39;s business products. This team is responsible for some of the highest-traffic, most security-critical surfaces at Coinbase, including sign-in, authentication, account management, and organization administration. You&#39;ll define how business customers manage users, roles, permissions, and security controls across Coinbase&#39;s growing product portfolio, directly shaping how enterprises adopt and scale on our platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the product roadmap for enterprise identity and multi-user capabilities, including role-based access control, organization management, SSO/SAML, domain claiming, and provisioning (SCIM, JIT).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the strategy for authentication, authorization, and account-security experiences that serve both consumer and business customers at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional launches by coordinating engineering, design, security, legal, privacy, CX, and international stakeholders through complex delivery milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Security and Engineering to identify vulnerabilities, define mitigations, and establish operational guardrails for privileged-access workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the long-term platform vision for identity primitives that unlock new business verticals and integrate across Coinbase&#39;s custodial product suite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product management experience with at least 2 years focused on identity, authentication, enterprise SaaS, or platform products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record shipping RBAC, SSO, MFA, or provisioning systems at scale in a B2B or multi-tenant environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to translate complex security and technical requirements into clear product strategies and intuitive user experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading launches that span security, privacy, legal, compliance, and customer-support stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in identity protocols and concepts (OAuth, SAML, OIDC, SCIM, session management, domain ownership) without requiring hands-on engineering ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
