&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Software Engineer, Backend on the Foundations, &lt;strong&gt;Settlements and Transfers team&lt;/strong&gt; within the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers/product-groups&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Institutional&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; group, you&#39;ll own the backend systems that power the secure movement of funds across fiat, crypto, and internal ledgers for Coinbase&#39;s institutional clients. This team is responsible for transaction processing, settlement, and asset transfer infrastructure that underpins the entire institutional platform. You&#39;ll drive technical direction, mentor engineers, and build the next generation of financial systems at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the design, build, and scaling of backend services that process settlements and transfers across fiat, crypto, and internal ledger systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive code quality and maintainability through rigorous code reviews, refactoring, and active participation across all stages of the development lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead performance and scalability improvements for critical financial infrastructure, including troubleshooting, triaging, and resolving production issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product managers, engineering managers, and cross-functional teams to translate product vision into quarterly technical roadmaps and deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Propose and implement architectural improvements that accelerate team velocity, reduce tech debt, and strengthen system reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor junior and mid-level engineers on technical best practices and professional growth, raising the bar across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required skills and experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of backend software engineering experience, including designing, building, and maintaining production services at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production experience with Go (or similar backend language), relational data stores (Postgres or equivalent), and message-based architectures (Kafka or equivalent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to own system design decisions, lead technical proposals, and drive alignment across a team of engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of identifying and resolving quality, performance, and scalability issues in distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring engineers and contributing to a culture of high code quality through thorough reviews, testing, and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
