&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Coinbase is building the future of regulated derivatives as part of the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/prime&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Institutional&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; Everything Exchange, and Coinbase Financial Markets (CFM) is our CFTC-regulated Futures Commission Merchant - the entity that lets retail and institutional clients trade and clear US futures and options. As a Staff Software Engineer on the FCM team, you&#39;ll be a hands-on technical anchor across the entire FCM lifecycle: market data, order entry and routing, settlement and money movement, back office reporting, and our in-house risk and liquidation system. You&#39;ll help lead a major replatforming onto next-gen architecture and reduce legacy vendor dependencies, a rare chance to re-architect a regulated trading platform from the inside, with the ownership of a startup and the reach of Coinbase.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own design and architecture across the FCM core, from market data and order routing through settlement, reporting, and risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the next-gen replatforming and reduce legacy vendor dependencies while raising stability and reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the technical bar through code, design reviews, and standards, and pay down the technical debt that matters most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner across pods (execution, risk, lifecycle) and cross-functionally with Product, CFM Risk and Ops, Finance, and Compliance to deliver correct, auditable systems and turn strategy into a roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers across the team and act as a force multiplier, elevating code quality and architectural rigor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required skills and experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of backend engineering experience, with demonstrated ownership of complex, production-grade distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct FCM or derivatives experience, with hands-on ownership of one or more parts of the futures trade lifecycle (settlement, clearing, margin/risk, order entry/routing, market data, or back office/books and records). Ion XTP or comparable exchange platform experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep proficiency in a modern backend language (Go preferred; Java or similar) and event-driven, high-availability architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a regulated or financial environment (CFTC/NFA or comparable) where correctness, auditability, and reliability are critical.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record delivering end-to-end - scoping, architecture, implementation, monitoring, and iteration - including replatforming or migrating off legacy systems, while still coding hands-on and raising the quality bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
